      "bullets": [
        "Beware over-abstraction; engineers often design overly generic, 50,000-foot meta-frameworks instead of solving immediate, concrete end-user problems.",
        "Joel Spolsky’s classic critique targets architectures like early SOAP and XML that prioritized theoretical purity over practical utility.",
        "Ground software systems in shipping code and actual user workflows rather than building endless abstraction layers for hypothetical future requirements."
      ]
